    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0607" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/5–646: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sands</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-05-06T09:00:00+03:06">May 6, 1946—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>129. (1) Sheikh Iusuf Yassin Deputy FonMin returned yesterday afternoon from
                    Riyadh and departed early this morning for Cairo where he will discuss Palestine
                    inquiry report with Arab League officials (Legtel 127, May 5<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d458-f1"/>). He told me on arrival only that the reaction of the
                    King to the report was “very bad”.</p>
                <p>(2) I am informed that staff members of British Legation here in conversation
                    with Saudis are successfully conveying impression that recommendation for entry
                    of hundred thousand Jews into Palestine was one purely of American origin
                    against which British members struggled unsuccessfully.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sands</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
